acceptance_criteria:
1) Service ingests runtime telemetry and token billing streams and emits validated hourly aggregates for route/model/customer within SLA of 15m;
2) Unit cost computation documented and reproducible: GPU seconds, memory weighting, kv-cache hits/evictions, and quantization multipliers are applied per-model;
3) Benchmarked throughput: can process 5M inference events/hour on a single cluster of service instances;
4) End-to-end tests assert parity vs. baseline sample aggregator for a 30-day replay within 2% for cost and 5% for latency percentiles;
5) Integrated with Console dashboard prototype (route-level cost+latency view) and visible to PM/finance;
6) Can toggle attribution granularity (route-only, route+model, route+model+customer) via config without service restart.

metrics_kpis:
- Processing latency: 95th percentile time from event ingestion to hourly aggregate available < 15 minutes;
- Accuracy: daily aggregate cost drift vs. replay baseline < 2%;
- Throughput: sustained processing of 5M events/hour with <2% message loss;
- Resource efficiency: cost per million events processed measured and reported;
- Rollout health: canary discrepancies count = 0 for critical metrics (cost, p50/p95 latency).
